    "SELECTION BIAS: realized outcomes (s1/s2/s3/msmi) exist ONLY for pairs the greedy collection policy actually introduced. Every outcome-based ranking statistic in this file conditions on that introduced subset, which was chosen by greedy priorities - not at random with respect to the features the model scores on.",
    "NO COUNTERFACTUAL LABELS: for feasible pairs that were never introduced in a validation state, no outcome is computed, imputed or assumed anywhere in this file. \"P_hat spread within a state\" is a score statement only; it says nothing about whether the high-scored edge would have outperformed the low-scored edge.",
