    "selection_bias_statement": "Outcomes exist ONLY for introduced pairs; these statistics are NOT top-k accuracy over all feasible pairs, and counterfactual outcomes of never-introduced pairs are never computed or imputed. See caveats.",
    "statistic_definition": "PAIRWISE CONCORDANCE (not Spearman rho; binary outcome ties make per-state rho degenerate). For each val state with >= 2 introduced pairs whose outcome y is decided (in {0,1}), every unordered pair of introduced pairs with y_i != y_j is COMPARABLE (outcome ties excluded). Each comparable pair scores 1.0 if sign(score_i - score_j) == sign(y_i - y_j) (concordant), 0.5 if score_i == score_j (prediction tie), else 0.0 (discordant). micro_concordant_share = total score / total comparable pairs, pooled over all states. macro_mean_per_state_concordance = unweighted mean over states of the per-state score share; states with zero comparable pairs (all outcomes tied) are excluded from the macro mean and from n_comparable_pairs."
